ratorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b12a7b7-1df3-5203-934e-8820604de3de" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d941e6-242a-56f2-a183-8415ae155e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d941e6-242a-56f2-a183-8415ae155e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265942} :answer-field/id #uuid "a25d2e89-0a5c-5d25-8fef-2f21d476c2a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265941} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb5ff408-2ffc-54dc-bed0-1bb557107473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb5ff408-2ffc-54dc-bed0-1bb557107473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265944} :answer-field/id #uuid "d54991f3-c7ea-52a5-9c51-98653f1fdaeb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265943}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7c36126f-c96f-583b-a972-fddac666ec65" :question/math-academy-id "q-332195" :question/problem "Express $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{5\\pi }{3})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{5\\pi }{3})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{5\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
